<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<archimate:model xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate" name="Active-Transfer-On-AKS-Example" id="id-241fb1177e824b9ea5b37a00bb96a79a" version="5.0.0">
  <folder name="Strategy" id="id-f1fd7f92dde24047a7345c8e5a8aed88" type="strategy"/>
  <folder name="Business" id="id-c88535a3afee4bfeb5f1bc7bc2e0dc77" type="business">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Security Team" id="id-biz-actor-secteam-00001">
      <documentation>Team responsible for creating foundational Azure identities and resource groups.
Responsibilities: Create and manage Azure AD identities, assign initial RBAC permissions, provide credentials to infrastructure team, manage identity lifecycle and secret rotation.
</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Infrastructure Team" id="id-biz-actor-infrateam-0002">
      <documentation>Team responsible for provisioning Azure infrastructure using Terraform.
Responsibilities: Provision Service Delivery resources (ACR, Key Vault, Azure DevOps), provision Service Fulfillment resources (AKS, SFTP VMs, PostgreSQL, App Gateway), use provided service principal credentials, request additional permissions if needed.
</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Application" id="id-6cf34d5ac80445418c2df7336cb8f392" type="application">
    <folder name="SecurityPrerequisites" id="id-app-secprereq-folder-00001">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Security Stage A - Prerequisites Core" id="id-app-secstageA-tf-000001">
        <documentation>Terraform project that creates foundational Azure resources before infrastructure provisioning.
Purpose: create a service principal for the infrastructure team to allow them provisioning, while still maintaining control to cover for normatives such as NIS2
Location: 01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/
Terraform Version: >= 1.0
Providers: azurerm (~> 4.0), azuread (~> 3.0), time (~> 0.12)
Managed By: Security Team
</documentation>
        <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
        <property key="terraform-version" value=">= 1.0"/>
        <property key="managed-by" value="Security Team"/>
        <property key="created-date" value="2026-07-21"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Security Stage A - Additional - option UAA" id="id-e21227c130eb4e379f4530a541744041">
        <documentation>If security principal may receive user access administration permissions, this is an option, however, in most organizations this is not allowed</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Security Stage A - Additional - option custom role" id="id-app-secstageA-custom-role-00001">
        <documentation>Alternative to UAA: creates a custom role definition granting only roleAssignments/write and /delete, then assigns it to the infra SP on both resource groups.
Required when the subscription Owner assignment carries an ABAC condition that blocks assigning built-in privileged roles (Owner, User Access Administrator, RBAC Administrator).
The custom role GUID is not in the ABAC deny-list, so the assignment succeeds.
This is also a better least-privilege design than UAA: the infra SP can only delegate within its own RGs.
Location: 01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/main.tf</documentation>
        <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
        <property key="managed-by" value="Security Team"/>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="InfrastructureProvisioning" id="id-app-infraprereq-folder-00001">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Infrastructure Stage B" id="id-app-infrastageB-tf-000001">
        <documentation>Terraform project that provisions Azure infrastructure resources for Service Delivery and Service Fulfillment.
Location: 01-azure-prerequisites/03-infra-stage-B/
Terraform Version: >= 1.0
Providers: azurerm (~> 4.0)
Managed By: Infrastructure Team
Resources: ~55 Azure resources (VNets, AKS, PostgreSQL, App Gateway, SFTP VMs, ACR, Storage, etc.)
</documentation>
        <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/03-infra-stage-B/"/>
        <property key="terraform-version" value=">= 1.0"/>
        <property key="managed-by" value="Infrastructure Team"/>
        <property key="created-date" value="2026-07-22"/>
        <property key="resource-count" value="~55"/>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="ServiceFulfillment" id="id-b094e814ab4d4eeaa44d72ad864b6eed">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT" id="id-396ebd509b99408e8a0452ff0687d361">
        <documentation>Managed File Transfer Service
Based on webMethods Active Transfer Technology
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT AKS" id="id-app-sf-aks-000000000006">
        <documentation>Azure Kubernetes Service cluster hosting the MFT workloads.
Provides container orchestration, workload identity (OIDC), Key Vault CSI driver and AGIC integration.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT AppGateway" id="id-app-sf-appgw-00000000007">
        <documentation>Azure Application Gateway acting as the ingress endpoint for the MFT solution.
Managed by AGIC (Application Gateway Ingress Controller) running inside AKS.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT Database" id="id-app-sf-postgres-0000008">
        <documentation>Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server providing the MFT transactional (mft_online) and archival (mft_archive) databases.
Deployed in a private subnet with no public network access.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT KeyVault SF" id="id-app-sf-keyvault-000000009">
        <documentation>Azure Key Vault holding runtime secrets for the MFT solution: certificates, database credentials, SFTP SSH keys and metering config.
Accessed by AKS pods via workload identity and the Key Vault CSI driver.

The security team is owning the vault, the application team mandated presence of keys. Operations and security team may alter values of the keys as needed.
</documentation>
        <property key="stability" value="medium-long term"/>
        <property key="owning team" value="security"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT SFTP LB" id="id-app-sf-lb-00000000000010">
        <documentation>Azure Standard Load Balancer providing a single public SFTP endpoint (port 55022) fronting the two SFTP gateway VMs.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT ATG VMs" id="id-app-sf-sftpvms-000000011">
        <documentation>Pair of Azure Linux Virtual Machines (sftp-vm-1, sftp-vm-2) acting as Active Transfer Gateway nodes.
Pull container images from ACR; expose service defined ports such as FTP, SFTP, FTPS and HTTP / HTTPS driven by the internal Active Transfer service and gateway ports to the AKS cluster so that the Active Transfer service can connect.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT VFS Storage" id="id-app-sf-storage-00000012">
        <documentation>Azure Storage Account (Azure Files, private endpoint only) providing the MFT Virtual File System (VFS) persistent volume.
Optional — enabled by the mft_vfs_private_enabled variable.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT Network SF" id="id-app-sf-network-0000000013">
        <documentation>Azure Virtual Network for the runtime platform: public subnets for SFTP VMs, private subnets for AKS and PostgreSQL, Application Gateway subnet.
Secured by NSGs per subnet.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT WorkloadIdentity" id="id-app-sf-identity-000000014">
        <documentation>Azure User-Assigned Managed Identity with federated credentials (OIDC) for the MFT Kubernetes service accounts.
Grants Key Vault access to MFT pods without storing credentials in the cluster.
</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="ServiceDelivery" id="id-5f5f53147e044e50b1c6020112f2e094">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT ACR" id="id-36f2bd3e10224074b745a791efbdbce9">
        <documentation>The example provides an Azure Container Registry to showcase the container images transport
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT KeyVault SD" id="id-app-sd-keyvault-000000000001">
        <documentation>Azure Key Vault used during the build and delivery phase to store secrets required by Azure DevOps pipelines and build agents.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT AgentPool Storage" id="id-app-sd-storage-000000000002">
        <documentation>Azure Storage Account with a large file share used by Azure DevOps self-hosted build agents for storing build artefacts and shared data.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT AgentPool" id="id-app-sd-vmss-0000000000003">
        <documentation>Azure VM Scale Set (uniform, 0 initial instances) providing self-hosted Azure DevOps build agents.
Scaled on demand by Azure DevOps to build and push container images to ACR.
</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Azure DevOps Agents VMSS" id="id-tech-sB-sd-vmss-00017">
        <documentation>Virtual Machine Scale Set for Azure DevOps self-hosted build agents.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachineScaleSets
Orchestration: Uniform
Initial Instances: 0 (scaled on demand)
Created By: Infrastructure Team (Stage B)
</documentation>
        <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachineScaleSets"/>
        <property key="created-by" value="Infrastructure Team (Stage B)"/>
        <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/03-infra-stage-B/"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MFT Network SD" id="id-app-sd-network-00000000005">
        <documentation>Azure Virtual Network, Subnet and NSG dedicated to the build agent VMSS.
Isolates agent traffic from the runtime platform network.
</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Technology &amp; Physical" id="id-cdf36429f3104aa2866ab552e5bf52bc" type="technology">
    <folder name="OwnedBySecurity" id="id-6592f07ff9424d3f9677568a27d5e912">
      <folder name="Identities" id="id-7b7a9d9c8b8145e383622132be6acdcb">
        <element xsi:type="archimate:SystemSoftware" name="${prefix}-agic-identity Managed Identity" id="id-tech-uami-agicidentity-00008">
          <documentation>User-Assigned Managed Identity for AGIC workloads running in AKS to manage Azure Application Gateway.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities
Resource Group: ${prefix}-s-fulfillment
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Optional: Can be disabled via create_agic_identity variable.
</documentation>
          <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities"/>
          <property key="resource-group" value="${prefix}-s-fulfillment"/>
          <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
          <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
          <property key="optional" value="yes — controlled by create_agic_identity variable"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:SystemSoftware" name="${prefix}-azdo-sp Azure AD Application" id="id-tech-app-azdoapp-00010">
          <documentation>Azure AD Application backing the Azure DevOps Stage C Service Principal.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.AzureActiveDirectory/applications
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Optional: Can be disabled via create_azdo_sp variable.
</documentation>
          <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.AzureActiveDirectory/applications"/>
          <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
          <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
          <property key="optional" value="yes — controlled by create_azdo_sp variable"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:SystemSoftware" name="${prefix}-infra-sp Service Principal" id="id-tech-sp-infrasp-0000003">
          <documentation>Service Principal used by infrastructure team for Terraform-based resource provisioning.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.AzureActiveDirectory/servicePrincipals
Authentication Type: Client Secret
Secret Validity: 1 year
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Purpose: Infrastructure provisioning automation
</documentation>
          <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.AzureActiveDirectory/servicePrincipals"/>
          <property key="authentication-type" value="Client Secret"/>
          <property key="secret-validity" value="1 year"/>
          <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
          <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
          <property key="secret-rotation-required" value="yes"/>
          <property key="next-rotation-date" value="2027-07-21"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:SystemSoftware" name="${prefix}-azdo-sp Service Principal" id="id-tech-sp-azdosp-00009">
          <documentation>Service Principal used by the DevOps/Application team for Stage C Azure DevOps service delivery provisioning.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.AzureActiveDirectory/servicePrincipals
Authentication Type: Client Secret
Secret Validity: 1 year
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Purpose: Azure DevOps service connection authentication against Azure
Optional: Can be disabled via create_azdo_sp variable.
</documentation>
          <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.AzureActiveDirectory/servicePrincipals"/>
          <property key="authentication-type" value="Client Secret"/>
          <property key="secret-validity" value="1 year"/>
          <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
          <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
          <property key="optional" value="yes — controlled by create_azdo_sp variable"/>
          <property key="secret-rotation-required" value="yes"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:SystemSoftware" name="${prefix}-infra-sp Azure AD Application" id="id-tech-app-infraapp-000004">
          <documentation>Azure AD Application backing the Infrastructure Team Service Principal.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.AzureActiveDirectory/applications
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
</documentation>
          <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.AzureActiveDirectory/applications"/>
          <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
          <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:SystemSoftware" name="${prefix}-mft-identity Managed Identity" id="id-tech-uami-mftidentity-00005">
          <documentation>User-Assigned Managed Identity for MFT workloads running in AKS to access Key Vault.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities
Resource Group: ${prefix}-s-fulfillment
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Optional: Can be disabled via create_mft_identity variable.
</documentation>
          <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities"/>
          <property key="resource-group" value="${prefix}-s-fulfillment"/>
          <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
          <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
          <property key="optional" value="yes — controlled by create_mft_identity variable"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="Azure Managed Identity" id="id-tech-identity-000000011">
          <documentation>Microsoft Azure managed identity service (User-Assigned Managed Identity with federated OIDC credentials).
Provides credential-free authentication from Kubernetes workloads to Azure services.
</documentation>
        </element>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Resources" id="id-2d918bfde001498396dcd5e5465d09c4">
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="${prefix}-s-delivery Resource Group" id="id-tech-rg-delivery-00000001">
          <documentation>Azure Resource Group for CI/CD infrastructure (ACR, Key Vault, Azure DevOps agents).
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Resources/resourceGroups
Purpose: Service Delivery
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
</documentation>
          <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Resources/resourceGroups"/>
          <property key="purpose" value="Service Delivery"/>
          <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
          <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="${prefix}-s-fulfillment Resource Group" id="id-tech-rg-fulfillment-000002">
          <documentation>Azure Resource Group for MFT runtime infrastructure (AKS, SFTP VMs, PostgreSQL, App Gateway).
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Resources/resourceGroups
Purpose: Service Fulfillment
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
</documentation>
          <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Resources/resourceGroups"/>
          <property key="purpose" value="Service Fulfillment"/>
          <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
          <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="Azure Key Vault" id="id-tech-keyvault-000000000001">
          <documentation>Microsoft Azure managed secrets, keys and certificates vault.
Used generically by both the ServiceDelivery (build-time) and ServiceFulfillment (runtime) modules — each has its own ApplicationService instance.
</documentation>
        </element>
      </folder>
      <folder name="AccessControl" id="id-73b12aa5138b4918b71b42b5842d341f">
        <folder name="StageA-Contributor" id="id-tech-ac-stageA-contributor-0001">
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Contributor on Service Delivery RG" id="id-tech-rbac-delivery-000006">
            <documentation>Role Assignment granting Infrastructure Team Service Principal Contributor permissions on Service Delivery Resource Group.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments
Role: Contributor
Scope: ${prefix}-s-delivery Resource Group
Principal: ${prefix}-infra-sp
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
</documentation>
            <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments"/>
            <property key="role" value="Contributor"/>
            <property key="scope" value="${prefix}-s-delivery Resource Group"/>
            <property key="principal" value="${prefix}-infra-sp"/>
            <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
            <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Contributor on Service Fulfillment RG" id="id-tech-rbac-fulfillmt-00007">
            <documentation>Role Assignment granting Infrastructure Team Service Principal Contributor permissions on Service Fulfillment Resource Group.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments
Role: Contributor
Scope: ${prefix}-s-fulfillment Resource Group
Principal: ${prefix}-infra-sp
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
</documentation>
            <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments"/>
            <property key="role" value="Contributor"/>
            <property key="scope" value="${prefix}-s-fulfillment Resource Group"/>
            <property key="principal" value="${prefix}-infra-sp"/>
            <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
            <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Contributor on Service Delivery RG for Azure DevOps" id="id-tech-rbac-azdo-delivery-00011">
            <documentation>Role Assignment granting Azure DevOps Service Principal Contributor permissions on Service Delivery Resource Group.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments
Role: Contributor
Scope: ${prefix}-s-delivery Resource Group
Principal: ${prefix}-azdo-sp
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Optional: Can be disabled via create_azdo_sp variable.
</documentation>
            <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments"/>
            <property key="role" value="Contributor"/>
            <property key="scope" value="${prefix}-s-delivery Resource Group"/>
            <property key="principal" value="${prefix}-azdo-sp"/>
            <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
            <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
            <property key="optional" value="yes — controlled by create_azdo_sp variable"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Reader on Key Vault RG" id="id-tech-rbac-keyvault-rg-00013">
            <documentation>Role Assignment granting Infrastructure Team Service Principal Reader permissions on Key Vault Resource Group.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments
Role: Reader
Scope: Key Vault Resource Group (from 01-vault/)
Principal: ${prefix}-infra-sp
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Optional: Can be disabled by not providing key_vault_resource_group_name variable.
Purpose: Allows infrastructure team to read Key Vault metadata for Terraform data sources without write access.
</documentation>
            <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments"/>
            <property key="role" value="Reader"/>
            <property key="scope" value="Key Vault Resource Group"/>
            <property key="principal" value="${prefix}-infra-sp"/>
            <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
            <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
            <property key="optional" value="yes — controlled by key_vault_resource_group_name variable"/>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="StageA-CustomRole" id="id-tech-ac-stageA-customrole-0002">
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="${prefix}-infra-role-delegator Custom Role Definition" id="id-tech-rbac-custom-roledef-00069">
            <documentation>Azure custom role definition granting only roleAssignments/write, /delete and /read.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Authorization/roleDefinitions
Scope: Subscription
Assignable Scopes: ${prefix}-s-delivery RG, ${prefix}-s-fulfillment RG, Key Vault RG (optional — when key_vault_resource_group_name is provided)
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Purpose: Replaces User Access Administrator to comply with enterprise subscription ABAC constraints that block assignment of built-in privileged roles (Owner, User Access Administrator, RBAC Administrator). Custom role has a distinct GUID not matched by the ABAC deny condition.
The Key Vault RG assignable scope is needed so the infra SP can assign Key Vault Secrets User, Certificate User and Administrator roles on the vault in Stage B.
</documentation>
            <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Authorization/roleDefinitions"/>
            <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
            <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
            <property key="abac-workaround" value="yes — custom GUID bypasses IBM ABAC condition"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="${prefix}-infra-role-delegator on Service Delivery RG" id="id-tech-rbac-delivery-custom-00070">
            <documentation>Role Assignment granting Infrastructure Team Service Principal the custom infra-role-delegator on Service Delivery Resource Group.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments
Role: ${prefix}-infra-role-delegator (custom)
Scope: ${prefix}-s-delivery Resource Group
Principal: ${prefix}-infra-sp
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Purpose: Allows infrastructure team to create role assignments within Service Delivery RG (e.g., AcrPull for VMs). Replaces UAA to comply with IBM ABAC policy.
</documentation>
            <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments"/>
            <property key="role" value="${prefix}-infra-role-delegator (custom)"/>
            <property key="scope" value="${prefix}-s-delivery Resource Group"/>
            <property key="principal" value="${prefix}-infra-sp"/>
            <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
            <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="${prefix}-infra-role-delegator on Service Fulfillment RG" id="id-tech-rbac-fulfillmt-custom-00071">
            <documentation>Role Assignment granting Infrastructure Team Service Principal the custom infra-role-delegator on Service Fulfillment Resource Group.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments
Role: ${prefix}-infra-role-delegator (custom)
Scope: ${prefix}-s-fulfillment Resource Group
Principal: ${prefix}-infra-sp
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Purpose: Allows infrastructure team to create role assignments within Service Fulfillment RG (e.g., AGIC roles, MFT Key Vault access). Replaces UAA to comply with IBM ABAC policy.
</documentation>
            <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments"/>
            <property key="role" value="${prefix}-infra-role-delegator (custom)"/>
            <property key="scope" value="${prefix}-s-fulfillment Resource Group"/>
            <property key="principal" value="${prefix}-infra-sp"/>
            <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
            <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="${prefix}-infra-role-delegator on Key Vault RG" id="id-tech-rbac-kv-custom-00072">
            <documentation>Role Assignment granting Infrastructure Team Service Principal the custom infra-role-delegator on Key Vault Resource Group.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments
Role: ${prefix}-infra-role-delegator (custom)
Scope: Key Vault Resource Group (from 01-vault/ — controlled by key_vault_resource_group_name variable)
Principal: ${prefix}-infra-sp
Created By: Security Team (Stage A)
Optional: only created when key_vault_resource_group_name variable is provided.
Purpose: Allows infrastructure team to create role assignments on the Key Vault in Stage B (Key Vault Secrets User for MFT identity, Key Vault Certificate User for MFT identity, Key Vault Administrator for Terraform). The Key Vault lives in a separate RG outside the two infra RGs — this third assignment is required.
</documentation>
            <property key="Azure Resource Type" value="Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments"/>
            <property key="role" value="${prefix}-infra-role-delegator (custom)"/>
            <property key="scope" value="Key Vault Resource Group"/>
            <property key="principal" value="${prefix}-infra-sp"/>
            <property key="created-by" value="Security Team (Stage A)"/>
            <property key="terraform-project" value="01-azure-prerequisites/02-sec-stage-A/"/>
            <property key="optional" value="yes — controlled by key_vault_resource_group_name variable"/>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="StageA-UAA-option" id="id-tech-ac-stageA-uaa-0003">
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="User Access Administrator on Service Delivery RG" id="id-tech-rbac-delivery-uaa-00067">
            <documentation>Role Assignment granting Infrastructure Team Service Principal User Access Administrator permissions on Service Delivery Resource Group.
Azure Resource Type: Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments
Role: User Access Administrator
Scope: ${prefix}-s-delivery Resource Group
Principal: ${prefix}-infra-sp
